### Start the app first with the local profile:
### ./gradlew bootRun --args='--spring.profiles.active=local'
### Postman users: import postman/ticketing-app.postman_collection.json instead.

@host = http://localhost:8085

### Book 2 seats: 201 with the booking. The id is kept for the next request.
POST {{host}}/events/rock-cluj/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerEmail": "ana@mail.ro", "seats": 2}

> {% client.global.set("bookingId", response.body.id); %}

### The booking just made
GET {{host}}/events/rock-cluj/bookings/{{bookingId}}

### The event's bookings, oldest first
GET {{host}}/events/rock-cluj/bookings

### An event with bookings cannot get fewer seats than it sold: 409 with bookedSeats
PUT {{host}}/events/rock-cluj
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Rock Night", "venueName": "BT Arena", "city": "Cluj", "startsAt": "2030-06-12T20:00:00", "capacity": 1}

### Cancel the booking just made: 204, and its seats go back to the event
DELETE {{host}}/events/rock-cluj/bookings/{{bookingId}}

### Cancelled: 404
GET {{host}}/events/rock-cluj/bookings/{{bookingId}}

### Call off an event that has bookings: create it, book it twice, delete it. The id is kept.
POST {{host}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Jazz Picnic", "venueName": "Parcul Central", "city": "Cluj", "startsAt": "2030-07-01T18:00:00", "capacity": 100}

> {% client.global.set("calledOffId", response.body.id); %}

### Ana books it
POST {{host}}/events/{{calledOffId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerEmail": "ana@mail.ro", "seats": 2}

### Ion books it
POST {{host}}/events/{{calledOffId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerEmail": "ion@mail.ro", "seats": 1}

### Move it to another date first: 200, and two "Booked event changed" lines in the log
PUT {{host}}/events/{{calledOffId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Jazz Picnic", "venueName": "Parcul Central", "city": "Cluj", "startsAt": "2030-07-08T18:00:00", "capacity": 100}

### Call it off: 204, and two "Booking cancelled … EVENT_CANCELLED" lines in the log
DELETE {{host}}/events/{{calledOffId}}

### Gone, with its bookings: 404
GET {{host}}/events/{{calledOffId}}/bookings

### Not enough seats: 409 with availableSeats
POST {{host}}/events/jazz-cluj/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerEmail": "ana@mail.ro", "seats": 500}

### Unknown event: 404
POST {{host}}/events/nope/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerEmail": "ana@mail.ro", "seats": 2}

### Zero seats: 400, the service is never called
POST {{host}}/events/rock-cluj/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerEmail": "ana@mail.ro", "seats": 0}
